 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518433,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the future value of an account if $450.00 per quarter is invested in a savings account bearing 3.5% interest compounded quarterly for 10 years.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$21,441.03"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The future value of an ordinary annuity is <span data-math=\"FV = pmt \\times \\frac{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}} - 1}}{{\\frac{r}{n}}}\"></span>, where <i>FV</i> is the future value of the annuity, <i>pmt</i> is the payment, <i>r</i> is the annual interest rate (in decimal form), <i>n</i> is the number of compounding periods per year, and <i>t</i> is the number of years. It is important to note that the number of deposits per year and the number of compounding periods per year must be the same.</p>\n<p>It will help you get the right answer using your calculator to find <span data-math=\"n \\times t\"></span> first.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n \\times t = \\left( 4 \\right) \\times \\left( {10} \\right) = 40\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"FV = 450 \\times \\frac{{\\left( {{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.035}}{4}} \\right)}^{40}} - 1} \\right)}}{{\\left( {\\frac{{0.035}}{4}} \\right)}} = \\$21,441.03\"></span></p>\n<p>The extra parentheses were added to help you enter the expression properly in your calculator.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
